Fix a null-pointer dereference in R2T2's streaming final flush.

R2T2ASRSession::build_stream_prefix(final_flush=true) clamps the rollback
end index to a minimum of 1 ("never roll back past the first token"), then
builds a std::vector<int32_t> from [ids.begin(), ids.begin() + end_index).
When `ids` is empty there is no first token: begin() is null and the range
constructor memmoves 4 bytes from address 0, killing the process with
SIGSEGV inside audiocpp_stream_finish().

`ids` is empty whenever raw_decoded_ has decoded to "" by the time the
stream is finished, which is reachable once chunk_id_ >= unfixed_chunk_num.
A forced request language makes that easy to hit: the "no <asr_text> tag
yet, nothing to commit" early-out in decode_stream_chunk() only applies when
force_language_ is empty, so chunk_id_ keeps advancing over chunks that
decode to nothing (silence, a trailing pause), and then any partial chunk
left in buffer_ sends finalize() down the final-flush path.

Reproduced deterministically with the C API: force a language, push four
320 ms chunks of silence plus a 2000-frame partial chunk, then call
audiocpp_stream_finish().

Applies to audio.cpp v0.8.2 (9bdd1d908bbd128e9eb405f5a8e38d0defb84c72).
Apply from the audio.cpp checkout root with `git apply`.

diff --git a/src/community_models/confucius4_r2t2/session.cpp b/src/community_models/confucius4_r2t2/session.cpp
index 68853c0a..aa618377 100644
--- a/src/community_models/confucius4_r2t2/session.cpp
+++ b/src/community_models/confucius4_r2t2/session.cpp
@@ -310,6 +310,14 @@ std::string R2T2ASRSession::build_stream_prefix(bool final_flush) const {
     if (final_flush) {
         // finish_streaming_transcribe uses a fixed rollback without the
         // replacement-character loop and never rolls back past the first token.
+        // There is no first token to keep when nothing has been decoded yet
+        // (silence, or a chunk that parsed down to an empty transcript while a
+        // forced language kept chunk_id_ advancing): clamping to 1 below would
+        // build a vector from [begin(), begin() + 1) on an empty vector, whose
+        // begin() is null.
+        if (ids.empty()) {
+            return {};
+        }
         const int64_t end_index = std::max<int64_t>(1, static_cast<int64_t>(ids.size()) - stream_config_.unfixed_token_num);
         return truncate_at_pipe(sanitize_utf8_lossy(tokenizer_.decode(std::vector<int32_t>(ids.begin(), ids.begin() + static_cast<std::ptrdiff_t>(end_index)))));
     }
